{
    "background_story": "In the Hundred Acre Wood, a string of mysterious honey jar thefts had the residents baffled. Enter Pooh, the unlikeliest of detectives. With his keen sense of smell and insatiable love for honey, Pooh set out to crack the case. He followed a trail of sticky clues, interviewing suspects like Rabbit, Tigger, and Eeyore along the way. Pooh's detective skills were surprisingly sharp, and he soon uncovered a surprising culprit: none other than his best friend, Piglet. It turned out that Piglet had been secretly collecting honey for a surprise birthday party for Pooh. With the case solved, Pooh was hailed as the Hundred Acre Wood's greatest detective, and his love for honey was once again satisfied.",
